      "field_id": "B.clinical_phenotypes",
      "value": "developmental regression after 6-18 months of relatively normal development; stereotypic hand movements (hand-wringing); tremors; gait apraxia; seizures (present in 58.8%); EEG abnormalities (87.5% of those tested); deceleration of head growth; ataxic cerebral palsy; autistic features; abnormal breathing pattern (hyperventilation and/or apnea); growth retardation (especially hands and feet); mild hypotonia in early developmental stage; loss of acquired purposeful hand skills; loss of language/speech (vocabulary limited to 4-5 words at most); loss of cognitive and motor abilities",
